{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  snippets/misc-access.liquid
  SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for "is this visitor approved to see
  commercial data" (prices, RRP, stock, ordering, asset password).

  Emits the string "true" or "false". Nothing else.

  Approved = the customer is a B2B company member (customer.b2b?)
             OR carries the customer tag `approved`.

  FAIL-SAFE: the result starts false and is only set true on a
  positive match. If `customer` is ever nil (logged out, or an
  unresolved session), this returns "false", so the worst case is
  an approved buyer briefly seeing the gated view, never an
  unapproved visitor seeing a price.

  Usage (compute once in a section, pass `approved` down to snippets):
    {%- capture misc_access -%}{%- render 'misc-access' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign misc_access = misc_access | strip -%}
    {%- assign approved = false -%}
    {%- if misc_access == 'true' -%}{%- assign approved = true -%}{%- endif -%}

  Trade-strict Liquid: no parentheses, no filter pipes inside if/elsif.
  The approval tag is lower-case `approved`. To change the word,
  change it here and in the banner block in layout/theme.liquid.
  ============================================================
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign misc_is_approved = false -%}
{%- if customer != blank -%}
  {%- if customer.b2b? -%}
    {%- assign misc_is_approved = true -%}
  {%- elsif customer.tags contains 'approved' -%}
    {%- assign misc_is_approved = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{{- misc_is_approved -}}
